# `u_nique` keeps the first of each distinct major cell, in first-seen
# order. `s_ort` orders major cells ascending, stably, comparing rows
# item by item; `g_rade` gives the 1-origin indices that sort, so
# `(g_rade v) s_elect v` is `s_ort v` (B7). Numbers and Chars are
# ordered (T8); `w_here` gives the indices of the 1s of a vector.
== SOURCE
u_nique 3 1 3 2 1
u_nique "mississippi"
u_nique 3 2 r_eshape 1 2 3 4 1 2
s_ort 3 1 4 1 5
s_ort "banana"
s_ort 3 2 r_eshape 2 1 1 9 1 3
s_ort 2.5 1 -3
g_rade 3 1 4 1 5
v := 3 1 4 1 5
(g_rade v) s_elect v
g_rade "cab"
w_here 0 1 1 0 1
w_here 3 1 4 1 5 > 2
t_ally w_here 0 0
t_ally s_ort 0 t_ake 1 2
